WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.400
Act 1: world night lights, 2012 to 2023. Each year, plucks sweep west to east; higher is further north, louder is brighter.

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:09.600
2023. Bells mark places brighter than in 2012, more each year.

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:13.800
Act 2, change. Purple, more light: high bells, mostly Asia and Africa.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:17.400
Then orange, less light: low plucks, as in parts of Europe.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:21.000
Third sweep: purple and orange together.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.000
Act 3: four regional zoom boxes.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:27.700
A tour, left to right: Western Europe, Eastern Mediterranean, Ukraine, India, each its own instrument.

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:36.800
The years run again in all four boxes. Bells mark brighter places. India and the Eastern Mediterranean brighten; Western Europe stays the same.

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:43.333
Final change, box by box: Western Europe mostly orange, the Eastern Mediterranean and Ukraine mixed, India almost all purple.
